1 0 0 1 74.00 710.50 Tm
(At her sister's wedding, Priya's aunties kept piling food on her plate. "Eat, eat - you're eating for) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 695.00 Tm
(two now!" By dessert she felt uncomfortable and a little guilty. Later, her doctor gently set her) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 679.50 Tm
(straight: eating for two doesn't mean twice the food - it means twice the care. "Your baby needs) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 664.00 Tm
(about one extra healthy snack a day, not a second dinner," she said. Priya felt a wave of relief.) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 648.50 Tm
(She didn't need to force down mountains of food. She just needed to make her normal meals) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 633.00 Tm
(count a little more.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 602.50 Tm
("Eating for two" is the most misunderstood phrase in pregnancy. Here is the truth that will save you a) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 586.00 Tm
(lot of stress: you only need about 300 extra calories per day - and only after the first trimester. That's) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 569.50 Tm
(roughly one nourishing snack, like a boiled egg and an apple, or a handful of nuts and some yogurt.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 547.00 Tm
(What matters far more than quantity is quality. Those 300 calories should be nutritious calories, not) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 530.50 Tm
(empty ones. A can of soda and a piece of fruit have similar calories, but only one of them builds a) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 514.00 Tm
(baby.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 491.50 Tm
(A note on healthy weight gain. Weight gain in pregnancy is normal, natural, and good - it's your body) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 475.00 Tm
(preparing for what's coming. General guidance \(always confirm with your provider\) looks like this:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 453.50 Tm
(- If you started at a normal weight: about 25-35 pounds total.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 438.00 Tm
(- If you started underweight: about 28-40 pounds.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 422.50 Tm
(- If you started overweight: about 15-25 pounds.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 407.00 Tm
(- If you're carrying twins: about 45-50 pounds.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 384.50 Tm
(In the first trimester, weight gain is usually small. Most of it comes later, especially in the second and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 368.00 Tm
(third trimesters as your baby grows quickly. Gaining steadily - rather than in sudden jumps - makes) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 351.50 Tm
(delivery easier and makes it far simpler to return to your pre-pregnancy weight afterward.) Tj
