0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 452.50 Tm
(Folate terrified Nadia - she kept reading the word "neural tube defect" and freezing. Her doctor) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 437.00 Tm
(turned it into a game instead. "For the next two weeks," she said, "just add one green thing to) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 421.50 Tm
(lunch and dinner. Spinach, broccoli, a handful of peas - anything." Nadia treated it like a little) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 406.00 Tm
(experiment. By the end of the fortnight it had become automatic; she barely noticed she was) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 390.50 Tm
(doing it. At her next appointment her bloodwork looked great, and the scary word had quietly lost) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 375.00 Tm
(its power over her.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 344.50 Tm
(Three nutrients do the heavy lifting early in pregnancy. Meet the Big Three.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 322.00 Tm
(Folate \(folic acid\) - the brain-and-spine builder. In early pregnancy your folate need roughly doubles.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 305.50 Tm
(It helps protect your baby from neural tube defects like spina bifida. Your provider will tell you the) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 289.00 Tm
(right supplement dose; alongside it, load up on folate-rich foods: dark leafy greens \(spinach, mustard) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 272.50 Tm
(greens, Romaine\), broccoli, Brussels sprouts, asparagus, green peas, avocado, beets; legumes) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 256.00 Tm
(\(lentils, chickpeas, black/kidney/white beans, edamame\); enriched breads, pasta, and breakfast) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 239.50 Tm
(cereals; berries and citrus; and seeds and nuts.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 217.00 Tm
(Iron - the oxygen courier. Iron builds the hemoglobin that carries oxygen to your baby \(and your own) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 200.50 Tm
(muscles\). In late pregnancy your baby draws on your iron reserves, and you'll lose some blood at) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 184.00 Tm
(delivery - so building iron now matters. Your body needs about 27 mg a day. Great sources: red) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 167.50 Tm
(meat, chicken, fish, egg yolks, lentils and beans, dark leafy greens, dried fruit \(prunes, raisins\), and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 151.00 Tm
(iron-enriched cereals.) Tj
0.720 0.470 0.100 rg
/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 114.50 Tm
(Two Iron Tricks Worth Knowing) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 80.00 99.50 Tm
(- Pair iron with vitamin C to absorb far more of it - squeeze lemon on your greens, or have an) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 80.00 84.50 Tm
(  orange, tomato, or grapefruit with an iron-rich meal.) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 80.00 69.50 Tm
(- Separate iron from calcium. Calcium blocks iron absorption, so don't take an iron supplement \(or) Tj
