/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 488.00 Tm
(By her fourth month, Fatima's morning sickness was gone - but a new problem appeared: she) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 472.50 Tm
(could no longer stand the smell of cooking meat, and meat had always been her main protein.) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 457.00 Tm
(She worried her baby's development would suffer. A friend who'd been through it grinned and) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 441.50 Tm
(handed her a shaker bottle. "You don't have to eat what turns your stomach," she said. "Whey) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 426.00 Tm
(protein shakes, eggs, beans, nuts, yogurt - there's more than one road to protein." Fatima blended) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 410.50 Tm
(fruit into a shake every morning and never looked at a steak again until well after the birth. Her) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 395.00 Tm
(baby arrived healthy and strong.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 364.50 Tm
(Welcome to the second trimester - for most mothers, the golden stretch. Morning sickness usually) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 348.00 Tm
(fades, energy returns, and appetite comes back. Now your baby's cognitive development) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 331.50 Tm
(accelerates, and the star nutrient of this season is protein.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 309.00 Tm
(Protein is the raw material of your baby - it builds every cell, supports rapid brain development, and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 292.50 Tm
(provides the amino acids your growing baby needs. It also does two lovely things for you: it curbs) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 276.00 Tm
(appetite and it evens out blood-sugar swings, which helps with cravings and energy crashes. Aim to) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 259.50 Tm
(include some protein in every meal and snack.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 237.00 Tm
(Good protein sources during pregnancy:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 215.50 Tm
(- Organic eggs - once feared for cholesterol, now recognized as an excellent source of protein and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 200.00 Tm
(    omega-3s.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 184.50 Tm
(- Organic meat - chicken and beef; choose organic to avoid added hormones.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 169.00 Tm
(- Seafood \(carefully chosen\) - a great source, but avoid high-mercury fish. Safer picks include) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 153.50 Tm
(    shrimp, salmon, sardines, anchovies, crab, and lobster. Keep to about two servings a week.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 138.00 Tm
(- Nuts and nut butters - perfect if meat turns you off; also rich in the healthy fats that build your) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 122.50 Tm
(    baby's brain.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 107.00 Tm
(- Legumes - beans, lentils, chickpeas, edamame.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 91.50 Tm
(- A whey protein shake - a genuine lifesaver on days when the smell of meat is unbearable.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 69.00 Tm
(Omega-3 fatty acids deserve a special mention here: they're vital for your baby's developing vision) Tj
